IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`

-- coa9-approval.l4: Companies Act 2006 (UK), Part 15 Chapter 9: quoted companies, members' approval of the directors' remuneration report
-- (ss 439, 439A, 440), lines 5852-5894 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: as in coa9-strategic.l4. A defence is answered as ruling (b) of 2026-11-05 says. Section 439(1A) and s 439A(8)(c)
-- are blank in this text, and s 440(5) has an elided definition before "existing director".
--
-- FINANCIAL YEARS. Section 439A counts financial years ("the first financial year which begins on or after ...", "the period of three
-- financial years beginning with the first financial year after ..."). This module numbers a company's financial years consecutively and
-- takes the number as an input (fork F29).
--
-- REGULATIVE RULE. Section 439(1) is also written as a regulative rule, `s 439(1) the quoted company must give notice ...`, run with #TRACE
-- in coa9-tests-approval.l4; its twin decision function is asserted, because a #TRACE adds no assertion line to the counts check.sh prints.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 439: Quoted companies: members' approval of directors' remuneration report
-- =========================================================================================================

§ `s 439 Quoted companies: members' approval of directors' remuneration report`

-- src:5853 | 439 Quoted companies ...: members' approval of directors' remuneration report
-- src:5854 | (1) A quoted company must, prior to the accounts meeting, give to the members of the company entitled to be sent notice of the meeting notice of the intention to move at the meeting, as an ordinary resolution, a resolution approving the directors' remuneration report for the financial yearother than the part containing the directors' remuneration policy (as to which see section 439A).
@ref s 439(1) A quoted company must give notice of the intention to move an ordinary resolution approving the directors' remuneration report (src:5853-5854)
GIVEN `s 385 the company is a quoted company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company has given, prior to the accounts meeting, to the members entitled to be sent notice of the meeting, notice of the intention to move at the meeting, as an ordinary resolution, a resolution approving the directors' remuneration report for the financial year other than the part containing the directors' remuneration policy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 439(1) the quoted company has given notice of the resolution approving the directors' remuneration report` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 385 the company is a quoted company`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a quoted company is decided by section 385
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A quoted company must"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the company has given, prior to the accounts meeting, to the members entitled to be sent notice of the meeting, notice of the intention to move at the meeting, as an ordinary resolution, a resolution approving the directors' remuneration report for the financial year other than the part containing the directors' remuneration policy`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a bare "must" not met, decided case by case, fork F32): "A quoted company must, prior to the accounts meeting, give to the members of the company entitled to be sent notice of the meeting notice of the intention to move at the meeting, as an ordinary resolution, a resolution approving the directors' remuneration report"

-- "prior to the accounts meeting" is read as strictly before the day of the meeting (fork F28): the last day for notice is the day before.
@ref s 439(1) (src:5854)
GIVEN `the date of the accounts meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 439(1) the last day on which the quoted company may give notice` MEANS
    `the date of the accounts meeting` MINUS 1

@ref s 439(1) (src:5854)
GIVEN `the day notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the date of the accounts meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 439(1) the quoted company gave notice prior to the accounts meeting` MEANS
    IF `the day notice was given` AT MOST `s 439(1) the last day on which the quoted company may give notice` `the date of the accounts meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a period fixed in the text's own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)): "prior to the accounts meeting"

@ref s 439(1) A quoted company must give notice of the intention to move an ordinary resolution approving the directors' remuneration report (src:5853-5854)
DECLARE `s 439(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 439(1) give notice of the intention to move the resolution`

@ref s 439(1) (src:5854)
GIVEN `the day the obligation arises` IS A DATE
      `the date of the accounts meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 439(1) action`
`s 439(1) the quoted company must give notice prior to the accounts meeting` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 439(1) give notice of the intention to move the resolution`
    WITHIN (Day (`s 439(1) the last day on which the quoted company may give notice` `the date of the accounts meeting`) MINUS Day `the day the obligation arises`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "notice of the intention to move the resolution approving the directors' remuneration report was not given prior to the accounts meeting"

-- src:5856 | (2) The notice may be given in any manner permitted for the service on the member of notice of the meeting.
@ref s 439(2) The notice may be given in any manner permitted for the service on the member of notice of the meeting (src:5856)
GIVEN `the manner is one permitted for the service on the member of notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 439(2) the notice may be given in the manner` MEANS
    IF `the manner is one permitted for the service on the member of notice of the meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any manner permitted for the service on the member of notice of the meeting"

-- src:5857 | (3) The business that may be dealt with at the accounts meeting includes the resolution.
-- src:5858 | This is so notwithstanding any default in complying with subsection (1) or (2).
@ref s 439(3) The business that may be dealt with at the accounts meeting includes the resolution, notwithstanding any default (src:5857-5858)
GIVEN `there is default in complying with subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 439(3) the business that may be dealt with at the accounts meeting includes the resolution` MEANS
    IF `there is default in complying with subsection (1) or (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- "This is so notwithstanding any default in complying with subsection (1) or (2)"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:5859 | (4) The existing directors must ensure that the resolution is put to the vote of the meeting.
@ref s 439(4) The existing directors must ensure that the resolution is put to the vote of the meeting (src:5859)
GIVEN `s 439(6) the person is an existing director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the resolution was put to the vote of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 439(4) the existing director has ensured that the resolution is put to the vote of the meeting` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 439(6) the person is an existing director`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the resolution was put to the vote of the meeting`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a bare "must" not met, decided case by case, fork F32): "The existing directors must ensure that the resolution is put to the vote of the meeting."
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The existing directors"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is an existing director was not answered

-- src:5860 | (5) No entitlement of a person to remuneration is made conditional on the resolution being passed by reason only of the provision made by this section.
@ref s 439(5) No entitlement to remuneration is made conditional on the resolution being passed by reason only of this section (src:5860)
GIVEN `the entitlement is made conditional on the resolution being passed by reason only of the provision made by section 439` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 439(5) the entitlement to remuneration is made conditional on the resolution being passed` MEANS
    IF `the entitlement is made conditional on the resolution being passed by reason only of the provision made by section 439`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No entitlement of a person to remuneration is made conditional on the resolution being passed by reason only of the provision made by this section."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only of the provision made by this section"; other reasons are not mentioned

-- src:5861 | (6) In this section—
-- src:5862 | “the accounts meeting” means the general meeting of the company before which the company's annual accounts for the financial year are to be laid; and
-- src:5863 | “existing director” means a person who is a director of the company immediately before that meeting.
@ref s 439(6) Meaning of "the accounts meeting" and "existing director" (src:5861-5863)
GIVEN `it is the general meeting of the company before which the company's annual accounts for the financial year are to be laid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 439(6) the meeting is the accounts meeting` MEANS
    IF `it is the general meeting of the company before which the company's annual accounts for the financial year are to be laid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the accounts meeting” means the general meeting of the company before which the company's annual accounts for the financial year are to be laid"

@ref s 439(6) (src:5861-5863)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the company immediately before that meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 439(6) the person is an existing director` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director of the company immediately before that meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“existing director” means a person who is a director of the company immediately before that meeting"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 439A: Quoted companies: members' approval of directors' remuneration policy
