§ `s 439A Quoted companies: members' approval of directors' remuneration policy`

-- src:5864 | 439A Quoted companies ...: members' approval of directors' remuneration policy
-- src:5865 | (1) A quoted company ... must give notice of the intention to move, as an ordinary resolution, a resolution approving the relevant directors' remuneration policy—
-- src:5866 | (a) at the accounts meeting held in the first financial year which begins on or after the day on which the company becomes a quoted company ..., and
@ref s 439A(1)(a) The quoted company must give notice at the accounts meeting in the first financial year that begins on or after the day it becomes a quoted company (src:5864-5866)
GIVEN `s 385 the company is a quoted company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the accounts meeting is held in the first financial year which begins on or after the day on which the company becomes a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 439A(1)(a) the quoted company must give notice of the intention to move the resolution approving the relevant directors' remuneration policy at the accounts meeting` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 385 the company is a quoted company`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a quoted company is decided by section 385
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A quoted company"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the accounts meeting is held in the first financial year which begins on or after the day on which the company becomes a quoted company`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a period fixed in the text's own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a); fork F35, other reading NOTHING): paragraph (a) names "the accounts meeting held in the first financial year which begins on or after" that day

-- src:5867 | (b) at an accounts or other general meeting held no later than the end of the period of three financial years beginning with the first financial year after the last accounts or other general meeting in relation to which notice is given under this subsection.
@ref s 439A(1)(b) Notice at a later meeting held no later than the end of three financial years after the last notice (src:5867)
GIVEN `the financial year number of the last accounts or other general meeting in relation to which notice is given under this subsection` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 439A(1)(b) the last financial year in which the next meeting at which notice is given may be held` MEANS
    `the financial year number of the last accounts or other general meeting in relation to which notice is given under this subsection` PLUS 3 -- the period of three financial years begins with the first financial year after that meeting's, so it ends with the third after it

@ref s 439A(1)(b) (src:5867)
GIVEN `the financial year number of the last accounts or other general meeting in relation to which notice is given under this subsection` IS A NUMBER
      `the financial year number of the accounts or other general meeting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 439A(1)(b) the meeting is held no later than the end of the period of three financial years` MEANS
    IF `the financial year number of the accounts or other general meeting` AT MOST `s 439A(1)(b) the last financial year in which the next meeting at which notice is given may be held` `the financial year number of the last accounts or other general meeting in relation to which notice is given under this subsection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a period fixed in the text's own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)): "at an accounts or other general meeting held no later than the end of the period of three financial years beginning with the first financial year after the last accounts or other general meeting in relation to which notice is given under this subsection"

-- src:5868 | (2) A quoted company ... must give notice of the intention to move at an accounts meeting, as an ordinary resolution, a resolution approving the relevant directors' remuneration policy if—
-- src:5869 | (a) a resolution required to be put to the vote under section 439 was not passed at the last accounts meeting of the company, and
-- src:5870 | (b) no notice under this section was given in relation to that meeting or any other general meeting held before the next accounts meeting.
@ref s 439A(2) The quoted company must give notice at the accounts meeting if the section 439 resolution was not passed and no notice has been given (src:5868-5870)
GIVEN `s 385 the company is a quoted company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a resolution required to be put to the vote under section 439 was not passed at the last accounts meeting of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no notice under section 439A was given in relation to that meeting or any other general meeting held before the next accounts meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 439A(2) the quoted company must give notice of the intention to move the resolution approving the relevant directors' remuneration policy at an accounts meeting` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 385 the company is a quoted company`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a quoted company is decided by section 385
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A quoted company"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `a resolution required to be put to the vote under section 439 was not passed at the last accounts meeting of the company`
           AND `no notice under section 439A was given in relation to that meeting or any other general meeting held before the next accounts meeting`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", reading (a) for a lawyer; fork F33): "must give notice of the intention to move at an accounts meeting ... if— (a) a resolution required to be put to the vote under section 439 was not passed at the last accounts meeting of the company, and (b) no notice under this section was given"

-- src:5871 | (2A) A quoted company ... must give notice of the intention to move at an accounts or other general meeting, as an ordinary resolution, a resolution approving the relevant directors’ remuneration policy if—
-- src:5872 | (a) a resolution required to be put to the vote under subsection (1) or (2) or this subsection was not passed at the last accounts or other general meeting of the company, and
-- src:5873 | (b) no notice under this section was given in relation to any other general meeting held before the next accounts meeting.
@ref s 439A(2A) The quoted company must give notice at an accounts or other general meeting if a resolution was not passed and no notice has been given (src:5871-5873)
GIVEN `s 385 the company is a quoted company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a resolution required to be put to the vote under subsection (1) or (2) or subsection (2A) was not passed at the last accounts or other general meeting of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no notice under section 439A was given in relation to any other general meeting held before the next accounts meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 439A(2A) the quoted company must give notice of the intention to move the resolution approving the relevant directors' remuneration policy at an accounts or other general meeting` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 385 the company is a quoted company`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a quoted company is decided by section 385
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A quoted company"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `a resolution required to be put to the vote under subsection (1) or (2) or subsection (2A) was not passed at the last accounts or other general meeting of the company`
           AND `no notice under section 439A was given in relation to any other general meeting held before the next accounts meeting`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", reading (a) for a lawyer; fork F33): "must give notice of the intention to move at an accounts or other general meeting ... if— (a) a resolution required to be put to the vote under subsection (1) or (2) or this subsection was not passed ..., and (b) no notice under this section was given"

-- src:5874 | (3) Subsection (2) does not apply in relation to a quoted company ... before the first meeting in relation to which it gives notice under subsection (1).
@ref s 439A(3) Subsection (2) does not apply before the first meeting for which the company gives notice under subsection (1) (src:5874)
GIVEN `the meeting is before the first meeting in relation to which the company gives notice under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 439A(3) subsection (2) does not apply in relation to the quoted company` MEANS
    IF `the meeting is before the first meeting in relation to which the company gives notice under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a period fixed in the text's own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a); fork F35, other reading NOTHING): "before the first meeting in relation to which it gives notice under subsection (1)"; at or after that meeting the exemption does not hold

-- src:5875 | (4) A notice given under subsection (2) or (2A) is to be treated as given under subsection (1) for the purpose of determining the period within which the next notice under subsection (1) must be given.
@ref s 439A(4) A notice under subsection (2) or (2A) is treated as given under subsection (1) for the period for the next notice (src:5875)
GIVEN `the financial year number of the last notice given under subsection (1)` IS A NUMBER
      `the financial year number of the last notice given under subsection (2) or (2A)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 439A(4) the financial year number treated as that of the last notice under subsection (1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the financial year number of the last notice given under subsection (2) or (2A)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the financial year number of the last notice given under subsection (1)`
    WHEN JUST laterNotice THEN max `the financial year number of the last notice given under subsection (1)` laterNotice

-- src:5876 | (5) Notice of the intention to move a resolution to which this section applies must be given, prior to the meeting in question, to the members of the company entitled to be sent notice of the meeting.
@ref s 439A(5) Notice must be given prior to the meeting to the members entitled to be sent notice of it (src:5876)
GIVEN `the resolution is one to which section 439A applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice was given, prior to the meeting in question, to the members of the company entitled to be sent notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 439A(5) notice of the intention to move the resolution was given as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the resolution is one to which section 439A applies`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a resolution to which this section applies"
    ELSE IF `notice was given, prior to the meeting in question, to the members of the company entitled to be sent notice of the meeting`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a bare "must" not met, decided case by case, fork F32): "Notice of the intention to move a resolution to which this section applies must be given, prior to the meeting in question, to the members of the company entitled to be sent notice of the meeting."

@ref s 439A(5) Notice must be given prior to the meeting to the members entitled to be sent notice of it (src:5876)
DECLARE `s 439A(6) subsection of section 439` IS ONE OF
    `s 439A(6) section 439(2) (manner of giving notice)`
    `s 439A(6) section 439(3) (business that may be dealt with)`
    `s 439A(6) section 439(4) (existing directors to ensure a vote)`
    `s 439A(6) another subsection of section 439`

-- src:5877 | (6) Subsections (2) to (4) of section 439 apply for the purposes of a resolution to which this section applies as they apply for the purposes of a resolution to which section 439 applies, with the modification that, for the purposes of a resolution relating to a general meeting other than an accounts meeting, subsection (3) applies as if for “accounts meeting” there were substituted “ general meeting ” .
@ref s 439A(6) Subsections (2) to (4) of section 439 apply to a resolution to which section 439A applies (src:5877)
GIVEN `the resolution is one to which section 439A applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      subsection IS A `s 439A(6) subsection of section 439`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 439A(6) the subsection of section 439 applies for the purposes of the resolution` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the resolution is one to which section 439A applies`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purposes of a resolution to which this section applies"
    ELSE CONSIDER subsection
         WHEN `s 439A(6) another subsection of section 439` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsections (2) to (4) of section 439"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 439A(6) (src:5877)
GIVEN `the resolution relates to a general meeting other than an accounts meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 439A(6) in section 439(3) "general meeting" is read for "accounts meeting"` MEANS
    IF `the resolution relates to a general meeting other than an accounts meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purposes of a resolution relating to a general meeting other than an accounts meeting"

@ref s 439A(6) Subsections (2) to (4) of section 439 apply to a resolution to which section 439A applies (src:5877)
DECLARE `s 439A(7) policy` IS ONE OF
    `s 439A(7)(a) the remuneration policy contained in the directors' remuneration report to be voted on at that accounts meeting`
    `s 439A(7)(b)(i) the remuneration policy contained in the directors' remuneration report voted on at the last accounts meeting before that other general meeting`
    `s 439A(7)(b)(ii) that policy as revised in accordance with section 422A`

-- src:5878 | (7) For the purposes of this section, the relevant directors' remuneration policy is—
-- src:5879 | (a) in a case where notice is given in relation to an accounts meeting, the remuneration policy contained in the directors' remuneration report in respect of which a resolution under section 439 is required to be put to the vote at that accounts meeting;
-- src:5880 | (b) in a case where notice is given in relation to a general meeting other than an accounts meeting—
-- src:5881 | (i) the remuneration policy contained in the directors' remuneration report in respect of which such a resolution was required to be put to the vote at the last accounts meeting to be held before that other general meeting, or
-- src:5882 | (ii) where that policy has been revised in accordance with section 422A, the policy as so revised.
@ref s 439A(7) The relevant directors' remuneration policy (src:5878-5882)
GIVEN `notice is given in relation to an accounts meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the policy contained in the report voted on at the last accounts meeting has been revised in accordance with section 422A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 439A(7) policy`
`s 439A(7) the relevant directors' remuneration policy` MEANS
    IF `notice is given in relation to an accounts meeting`
    THEN `s 439A(7)(a) the remuneration policy contained in the directors' remuneration report to be voted on at that accounts meeting`
    ELSE IF `the policy contained in the report voted on at the last accounts meeting has been revised in accordance with section 422A`
         THEN `s 439A(7)(b)(ii) that policy as revised in accordance with section 422A`
         ELSE `s 439A(7)(b)(i) the remuneration policy contained in the directors' remuneration report voted on at the last accounts meeting before that other general meeting`

-- src:5883 | (8) In this section—
-- src:5884 | (a) “ accounts meeting ” means a general meeting of the company before which the company's annual accounts for a financial year are to be laid;
@ref s 439A(8)(a) Meaning of "accounts meeting" in section 439A (src:5883-5884)
GIVEN `it is a general meeting of the company before which the company's annual accounts for a financial year are to be laid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 439A(8)(a) the meeting is an accounts meeting` MEANS
    IF `it is a general meeting of the company before which the company's annual accounts for a financial year are to be laid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“ accounts meeting ” means a general meeting of the company before which the company's annual accounts for a financial year are to be laid"

-- src:5885 | (b) “directors' remuneration policy” means the policy of the company with respect to the matters mentioned in section 421(2A);
@ref s 439A(8)(b) Meaning of "directors' remuneration policy" in section 439A (src:5885)
GIVEN `the policy is the policy of the company with respect to the matters mentioned in section 421(2A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 439A(8)(b) the policy is a directors' remuneration policy` MEANS
    IF `the policy is the policy of the company with respect to the matters mentioned in section 421(2A)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“directors' remuneration policy” means the policy of the company with respect to the matters mentioned in section 421(2A)"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 440: Quoted companies: offences in connection with procedure for approval
-- =========================================================================================================

§ `s 440 Quoted companies: offences in connection with procedure for approval`

-- src:5887 | 440 Quoted companies ...: offences in connection with procedure for approval
-- src:5888 | (1) In the event of default in complying with section 439(1)or 439A(1), (2) or (2A) (notice to be given of resolution for approval of directors' remuneration reportor policy), an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 440(1) An officer in default commits an offence if notice is not given (src:5887-5888)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 439(1) or 439A(1), (2) or (2A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 440(1) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`default is made in complying with section 439(1) or 439A(1), (2) or (2A)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", reading (a) for a lawyer): "In the event of default in complying with section 439(1) or 439A(1), (2) or (2A) ..., an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is decided by section 1121

-- src:5889 | (2) If the resolution is not put to the vote of the meeting to which it relates, an offence is committed by each existing director.
